#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0222 expect=violation domain=TA
#note "Authority: SEND Conformance Rules v5.0 SEND222, Rule 'TA.ETCD = TE.ETCD'; Plain Text: 'The values of ETCD used in the Trial Arms dataset must match values for the same Element in the Trial Elements dataset.' Row 5: arm 2's third element uses ETCD=RECOV2, which TE does not define (TE has SCRN, TRT, RECOV) -> FIRES. Rows 1-4 use TE codes -> silent. ALSO THE S3 FOREIGN-DISCRIMINATION PIN (SKELETON-distinct-function hazard 3): RECOV2 exists only in the primary TA, so a port that read ETCD from TA instead of TE would find row 5's own value in its own set and fall silent."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=5 ARMCD=2 ETCD=RECOV2
dataset TA label="Trial Arms"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col TAETORD type=Num  label="Order of Element within Arm"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col EPOCH   type=Char label="Epoch"
---
S1 | TA | 1 | Control   | 1 | SCRN   | Screening | SCREENING
S1 | TA | 1 | Control   | 2 | TRT    | Treatment | TREATMENT
S1 | TA | 2 | High Dose | 1 | SCRN   | Screening | SCREENING
S1 | TA | 2 | High Dose | 2 | TRT    | Treatment | TREATMENT
S1 | TA | 2 | High Dose | 3 | RECOV2 | Recovery  | RECOVERY
---

dataset TE label="Trial Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col TESTRL  type=Char label="Rule for Start of Element"
---
S1 | TE | SCRN  | Screening | First day of acclimation
S1 | TE | TRT   | Treatment | First dose
S1 | TE | RECOV | Recovery  | Day after last dose
---
